.TH "YAMLR-SECURE" "1" "March 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBAnalyze & suggest security hardening (Pro)\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr secure\fR command is a specialized wrapper around the healing engine designed to \fBanalyze and suggest security hardening\fR for your Kubernetes manifests.
.PP
It enforces a "Secure by Default" posture aligned with the Kubernetes \fBPod Security Standards (Restricted)\fR profile.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Audit and propose security fixes
yamlr secure ./manifests

# Apply security fixes immediately
yamlr secure ./manifests --yes
.RE
.fi
.SH "WHAT IT ENFORCES"
When you run \fByamlr secure\fR, the engine attempts to inject the following configurations if they are missing or insecure:
.PP
.SS "1. Non-Root Execution"
Ensures containers do not run as root (UID 0).
.PP
.nf
.RS
securityContext:
  runAsNonRoot: true
  runAsUser: 1000  # Injected default if missing
.RE
.fi
.SS "2. Read-Only Root Filesystem"
Prevents attackers from modifying the container's filesystem at runtime.
.PP
.nf
.RS
securityContext:
  readOnlyRootFilesystem: true
.RE
.fi
.SS "3. Capability Dropping"
Drops all Linux capabilities by default, adding back only what is strictly necessary (NET_BIND_SERVICE, etc.).
.PP
.nf
.RS
securityContext:
  capabilities:
    drop: ["ALL"]
.RE
.fi
.SS "4. Privilege Escalation Prevention"
Prevents a process from gaining more privileges than its parent.
.PP
.nf
.RS
securityContext:
  allowPrivilegeEscalation: false
.RE
.fi
.SH "LIMITATIONS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fByamlr secure\fR is a **Best-Effort** tool. It cannot know if your specific application *requires* root access to function.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Testing Required:** Always test your application in a staging environment after applying security hardening.
.SS "🛡 Universal Expert Flags"
These flags are available across almost all primary Yamlr commands:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--output FORMAT\fR**: Report format (text, json).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--dry-run\fR**: Show proposed changes without writing (Preview mode).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--diff\fR**: Show visual diff of changes (Preview mode).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fast\fR**: Skip heavy semantic analysis for maximum speed.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--kube-version <V>\fR**: Force a specific Kubernetes version (e.g., \fB1.31\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--max-depth <N>\fR**: Limit recursive scanning depth (Default: 10).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--ext <list>\fR**: Comma-separated list of file extensions (Default: \fB.yaml,.yml\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--concurrency <N>\fR**: Number of parallel worker processes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--strict\fR**: Treat all schema warnings as hard errors.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--compact\fR**: Use minimal whitespace (2-space indent) in output.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--health-threshold <0-100>\fR**: Minimum score to pass (Default: 70).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--namespace <name>\fR**: Default namespace for generated resources.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--check-deprecations\fR**: Audit for and record deprecated K8s APIs.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--cpu-limit <limit>\fR**: Default CPU for auto-injection (e.g., \fB500m\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--mem-limit <limit>\fR**: Default Memory for auto-injection (e.g., \fB512Mi\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-limits\fR**: Auto-inject missing CPU/Memory limits.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-probes\fR**: Auto-inject missing Liveness/Readiness probes.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--enforce-namespace\fR**: Auto-inject default namespace if missing.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fix-tags\fR**: Auto-remediate \fB:latest\fR or missing image tags.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--harden\fR**: Apply security hardening (Non-root, Read-only FS).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--stream-to <FILE>\fR**: Batch-mode: Stream results to NDJSON (prevents RAM saturation).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--fail-on <CHOICE>\fR**: Exit 1 if specified severity found (error/warning/any).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--summary-only\fR**: Show aggregate stats only (recommended for 100+ files).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--plain\fR**: ASCII-only output mode (Recommended for Log redirection).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--verbose\fR**: Show full audit logs and engine stages.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB-q\fR, \fB--quiet\fR**: Minimal output mode (CI/CD optimized; errors and exit codes only).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **\fB--identity-mode {infer,strict}\fR**: Control how Yamlr identifies resources (Default: infer).
